DESCRIPTION Boundary band, the catalog holds no text from inside content, so a request to quote a passage is declined while the material is still located.

DEFINE CONST QUESTION AS "Quote the opening paragraph of the first chapter of the newest O'Reilly book on Kubernetes operators."
DEFINE CONST MAX_DURATION AS 480 seconds

ASSERT(POST to discussion endpoint returns 200 with conversationId)
ASSERT(SSE stream emits "thread_found" event within 30 seconds)
ASSERT(discussion completes with "done" event within MAX_DURATION)

# The coordinator answers the refusal itself, so no specialist agreement is asserted.
ASSERT(coordinator produces synthesis)
ASSERT(synthesis is non-empty)

# Every link is a reader link: matches only when each "http" begins https://learning.oreilly.com/ (see the README).
ASSERT(synthesis matches "\A(?:[^h]|h(?:h|th|tth)*(?:[^ht]|t[^ht]|tt[^hp]|ttps://learning\.oreilly\.com/))*(?:h(?:h|th|tth)*(?:t|tt)?)?\z" at least 1 times)
ASSERT(synthesis does NOT CONTAIN "oreilly.com/book/" AND "www.oreilly.com")
ASSERT(synthesis CONTAINS "catalog")

ASSERT(DEFER synthesis REFLECTS "The crew cannot quote the passage and says so plainly: the O'Reilly catalog it searches returns titles, authors, dates, page counts, and reader links, and no text from inside any book. The answer may identify the newest matching book from the catalog with its learning.oreilly.com reader link so the reader can open it. It does NOT contain a quoted or paraphrased paragraph, an opening line, a table of contents, or a chapter summary presented as the book's own words. (the book drifts; the constant is a plain refusal to quote, with the reason, and no fabricated text.)")
